  "question": {
    "text": "If the distance of the point $P(1,-2,1)$ from the plane $x+2 y-2 z=\\alpha$, where $\\alpha>0$, is 5 , then the foot of the perpendicular from $P$ to the plane is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ViC49",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\frac{8}{3}, \\frac{4}{3},-\\frac{7}{3}\\right)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "zB20A",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\frac{4}{3},-\\frac{4}{3}, \\frac{1}{3}\\right)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ldjbO",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\frac{1}{3}, \\frac{2}{3}, \\frac{10}{3}\\right)$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "T9wrx",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\frac{2}{3},-\\frac{1}{3}, \\frac{5}{2}\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\text { Distance of point } P \\text { from plane }=5\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\n\\therefore=\\left|\\frac{1-4-2-\\alpha}{3}\\right| \\\\\n\\alpha=10\n\\end{gathered}\n$$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/MOxuxyIje_ig706wFu1-BnuXYO0fzZdi-AYRS4GoBC8.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\nFoot of perpendicular\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\quad \\frac{x-1}{1} & =\\frac{y+2}{2}=\\frac{z-1}{-2}=\\frac{5}{3} \\\\\n\\Rightarrow \\quad \\quad \\quad x & =\\frac{8}{3}, y=\\frac{4}{3}, z=-\\frac{7}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nThus, the foot of the perpendicular is\n$$\nA\\left(\\frac{8}{3}, \\frac{4}{3},-\\frac{7}{3}\\right)\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
